hadiths[114]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1238","The Prophet Muhammad, peace and blessings be upon him, came to meet him and asked: “O Thumamah! What is in your mind?” He replied: “If you kill me, then you will be killing a person who has shed blood, and if you show kindness, you will be showing kindness to a grateful person, and if you want wealth, then whatever you desire will be given to you.” The narrator states: The companions of the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, preferred the option of taking ransom. They said: “What will we gain by killing him?” Then one day, the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, passed by him and he accepted Islam. The Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, sent him to the garden of Abu Talhah and instructed that he should perform ghusl (ritual bath). He performed ghusl and offered two rak‘ahs of prayer. The Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, said: “The Islam of your companion is excellent.”"
"1239","The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent some horsemen to Najd. They captured a man. He was from the tribe of Banu Hanifa and was called Thumama b. Uthal. He was the chief of the people of Yamama. People bound him with one of the pillars of the mosque. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came out to (see) him. He said: O Thumama, what do you think? He replied: Muhammad, I have good opinion of you. If you kill me, you will kill a person who has spilt blood. If you do me a favour, you will do a favour to a grateful person. If you want wealth, ask and you will get what you will demand. The Messenger of Allah (may peace be pon him) lefthim (in this condition) for two days, (and came to him again) and said: What do you think, O Thumama? He replied: What I have already told you. If you do a favour, you will do a favour to a grateful person. If you kill me, you will kill a person who has spilt blood. If you want wealth, ask and you will get what you will demand. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ left him until the next day when he (came to him again) and said: What do you think, O Thumama? He replied: What I have already told you. If you do me a favour, you will do a favour to a grateful person. If you kill me, you will kill a person who has spilt blood. If you want wealth ask and you will get what you will demand. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: Set Thumama free. He went to a palm-grove near the mosque and took a bath. Then he entered the mosque and said: I bear testimony (to the truth) that there is no god but Allah and I testify that Muhammad is His bondman and His messenger. O Muhammad, by Allah, there was no face on the earth more hateful to me than your face, but (now) your face has become to me the dearest of all faces. By Allah, there was no religion more hateful to me than your religion, but (now) your religion has become the dearest of all religions to me. By Allah, there was no city more hateful to me than your city, but (now) your city has become the dearest of all cities to me. Your horsemen captured me when I intended going for Umra. Now what is your opinion (in the matter)? The Messenger of Allah ﷺ announced good tidings to him and told him to go on 'Umra. When he reached Mecca, somebody said to him: Have you changed your religion? He said: No! I have rather embraced Islam with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. By Allah, you will not get a single grain of wheat from Yamama until it is permitted by the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. (Using translation from Muslim 1764a)"
"1240","It was narrated from Qais bin 'Asim that he accepted Islam, and the Prophet commanded him to perform Ghusl with water and lotus leaves. (Using translation from Nasāʾī 188)"
"1241","narrates this statement of the Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him): ""Nothing makes water impure."
"1242","The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came and began to perform wudu (ablution) with the water she had left over. That woman said to him: (This is the leftover water from my ghusl.) The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Nothing makes water impure."
"1243","The Prophet (peace be upon him) said: Its water is pure and its dead (animals) are lawful."
"1244","""Its water is pure (and Purification) and its 'dead meat' is permissible (to eat)."" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 4350)"
"1245","It was narrated from Umm Hani' that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ performed Ghusl, he and Maimunah from a single vessel, a bowl in which there were traces of dough. (Using translation from Nasāʾī 240)"
"1246","when a fly alights in anyone’s vessel, he should plunge it all in, for in one of its wings there is a disease, and in the other is a cure. It prevents the wing of it is which there is a cure, so plunge it all in (the vessel). (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 3844)"
"1247","narrates this statement of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): ""When a fly falls into the vessel of any person, then immerse it completely, for indeed in one of its wings is disease, and in the other is cure."
"1248","One of the wives of the Prophet ﷺ took a bath from a large bowl. The Prophet ﷺ wanted to perform ablution or take from the water left over. She said to him: O Prophet of Allah, verily I was sexually defiled. The Prophet said: Water not defiled. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 68)"
"1249","""The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was asked about water and how some animals and carnivorous beasts might drink from it. He said: 'If the water is more than two Qullahs, it will not carry filth.'""[1] [1]It comes with some explanation in Sunan At Timidhi 'Abdah (one of the narrators) said: ""Muhammad bin Ishaq said: 'A Qullah refers to Jirar (These are two nouns describing large casks that are used to hold water), and a Qullah is the thing that drinking water is held in.""' At-Tirmidhi said: ""This is the saying of Ash Shafa'i, Ahmad and Ishaq. They say that when the water is two Qullahs then nothing makes it impure, as long as it does not change its smell, and its taste. And they say, it is approximately fifty Qirbahs (waterskins)."" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 52)"
"1250","The Messenger of Allah forbade urinating into standing water. (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 343)"
"1251","the Prophet said: ""Let none of you urinate [in still water, then perform Wudu with it.""1 (Using translation from Tirmidhī 68)"
"1252","Abu Sa'ib, the freed slave of Hisham bin Zuhrah, told him that he heard Abu Hurairah say: ""The Messenger of Allah said: 'No one of you should bathe in standing water when he is sexually impure.'"" He (Abu Sa'ib) said: ""What should he do, O Abu Hurairah?"" He said: ""Let him take some out (and pour it over himself)."" (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 605)"
"1253","The Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) was asked about such water from which wild beasts and animals also come and drink. The Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) said: ""When the water reaches two qullahs, nothing makes it impure."" (Imam Ibn Hibban, may Allah have mercy on him, says:) These words are for conveying information. It means to inform about the thing that was asked about. Its meaning is that none of the things about which the question was asked make it impure."
"1254","""You should not pass urine in stagnant water which is not flowing then (you may need to) wash in it."" (Using translation from Bukhārī 239)"
"1255","The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade that a person should urinate at the place where he bathes, because usually this causes doubts (whispers/waswasah) to arise."
"1256","the Prophet said: ""Let none of you urinate [in still water, then perform Wudu with it.""1 (Using translation from Tirmidhī 68)"
"1257","The Prophet ﷺ said: None amongst you should urinate in standing water, then wash in it after sexual defilement. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 70)"
"1258","""When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ met a man from among his Companions, he would shake hands with him and supplicate for him. I saw him one day in the early morning, and I tried to avoid him, then I came to him later in the day. He said: 'I saw you but you were avoiding me.' I said: 'I was Junub and I was afraid that you would touch me.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'The Muslim is not made impure (Najis).'"" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 267)"
"1259","I was in a state of major ritual impurity (janabah). I continued walking with him, and he was holding my hand. Then I left from his presence, performed ghusl (ritual bath), and returned to him and sat with him. The Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, asked: O Abu Hurairah, where did you go? I replied: When you met me, I was in a state of janabah, and I did not like to sit with you in that condition. The Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, said: Indeed, a believer is never impure."
"1260","The Messenger of Allah forbade men to perform ablution with the left over water by a woman. (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 373)"
"1261","""One of the wives of the Prophet performed Ghusl with a bowl. Messenger of Allah wanted to perform Wudu with it, so she said: 'O Messenger of Allah! Indeed I am ]unub.' So he said: 'Indeed, water does not become Junub.'"" (Using translation from Tirmidhī 65)"
"1262","""I heard Al-Qasim narrating that 'Aishah said: 'I used to perform Ghusl, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and I from a single vessel, from Janabah.'"" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 233)"
"1263","narrates: He saw the Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) and his companions, that they, meaning a man and a woman (i.e., husband and wife), would perform ablution from the same vessel. All of them would attain purification from it."
"1264","""I heard Al-Qasim narrating that 'Aishah said: 'I used to perform Ghusl, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and I from a single vessel, from Janabah.'"" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 233)"
"1265","narrates: In the blessed era of the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him), men and women (that is, husband and wife) used to perform ablution together."
"1266","I was ill and I was unconscious at that time. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed ablution and sprinkled the leftover water of his ablution on me. I said: O Messenger of Allah! (To whom) will my inheritance go, because my inheritance is in the form of kalalah (having no direct heirs)? Then the verse regarding the ruling of inheritance was revealed. (Imam Ibn Hibban, may Allah have mercy on him, says:) The Prophet’s (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) act of sprinkling the leftover water of his ablution on Sayyiduna Jabir is a clear statement that the water with which ablution has been performed is pure, and whoever has access to this water is not permitted to perform tayammum, because he will be considered as one who has found pure water, and Allah Almighty has permitted tayammum only when water is not available, so how can a person who has found pure water perform tayammum?"
"1267","The Prophet’s (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sufficing with one vessel for the face and both hands while teaching tayammum is a clear statement that it is permissible to perform another obligatory act with that by which one obligatory act has been performed. Its form is that it is obligatory for the person performing tayammum to wipe his face and both hands. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) has permitted for both hands in tayammum that which remains (of dust) on his palm after performing the obligatory act for the face, so it is correct that the earth by which the obligatory act of one vessel has been performed, it is permissible to perform the obligatory act of another vessel with it in the second time. So when this is correct in tayammum, it will also be correct in wudu.)"
"1268","Sayyiduna Bilal (may Allah be pleased with him) come out carrying the leftover water from the Prophet’s ablution. I saw people rushing towards the leftover water of ablution and they began to rub it on their bodies. Then Sayyiduna Bilal (may Allah be pleased with him) came out carrying a spear. He fixed it in the ground. Then the Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) came out wearing a red Yemeni cloak. He faced towards the spear and performed prayer, while people and animals were passing on the other side of it."
"1269","One of the wives of the Prophet ﷺ took a bath from a large bowl. The Prophet ﷺ wanted to perform ablution or take from the water left over. She said to him: O Prophet of Allah, verily I was sexually defiled. The Prophet said: Water not defiled. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 68)"
"1270","I brought milk to the service of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) which was not covered. At that time, you were at the place of ""Naqi‘"". You said: Why did you not cover it? Even if you had placed a stick over it. Sayyiduna Abu Humayd (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: We were commanded regarding vessels that at night their mouths should be closed, and regarding doors, we were commanded that at night they should be closed."
"1271","narrates this statement of the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""(At night when going to sleep) close the doors, tie the mouths of the water skins, cover the vessels, and extinguish the lamps, because the devil does not open closed doors, does not untie the mouths of tied water skins, does not remove the cover from vessels, and sometimes a mouse sets people's houses on fire."
"1272","Shut your door and make mention of Allah's name, for the devil does not open a door which has been shut; extinguish your lamp and make mention of Allah's name, cover up your vessel even by a piece of wood that you just put on it and make mention of Allah's name, and tie up your water-skin mentioning Allah's name. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 3731)"
"1273","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) commanded us with four things, and forbade us from five things. (He said:) When you go to sleep, close your door, tie the mouth of your water-skin, cover your vessel, and extinguish your lamp, because Satan does not open a closed door, does not untie a tied water-skin, does not uncover a covered vessel, and sometimes a mouse sets the house on fire along with its inhabitants. And do not eat with your left hand, do not drink with your left hand, do not walk wearing only one shoe, do not wear your garment in the manner of ishtimal as-samma’ (wrapping it tightly around the body), and do not sit in your house in such a way with your garment that your private parts become exposed."
"1274","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) used to say: ""Close the mouth of the water-skin when you go to sleep at night, and cover food and drink, because the devil comes; if he finds a door not closed, he enters, and if he finds the mouth of a water-skin not closed, he drinks from it. But if he finds the door closed, or the mouth of the water-skin closed, he cannot open the closed mouth of the water-skin nor the closed door. And if a person does not find anything to cover his vessel in which his drink is, then he should place even a piece of wood over it."
"1275","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said to us, ""Close your doors, tie the mouths of your water-skins, cover your vessels, and extinguish your lamps, for indeed Satan does not open a closed door, nor untie a tied water-skin, nor uncover a covered vessel, and sometimes a mouse sets the house on fire along with its inhabitants. Keep your livestock and family members inside the house near sunset until the early part of the night has passed."
"1276","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Keep your livestock (inside the house) confined until the early part of the night passes, because this is an hour in which Satan sets fire."
"1277","""The Messenger of Allah wrote to us: 'Do not make use of the skins and sinew of dead animals.""' (Using translation from Nasāʾī 4250)"
"1278","The letter of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was read out to us in the territory of Juhaynah when I was a young boy: Do not make use of the skin or sinew of an animal which died a natural death. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 4127)"
"1279","The words of the narration transmitted by Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Ukeem, ""Do not benefit from the skin or sinew of a dead animal,"" mean that you should not do so before tanning. The evidence for this being correct is the statement of the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him): ""Any skin that is tanned becomes pure."
"1280","I do not find within that which was revealed to me [anything] forbidden to one who would eat it unless it be a dead animal..."" He recited the verse to its end (then he said): People are not eating it. Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) narrates: Then that woman sent the skin, it was tanned, and a water bag was made from its skin. Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) narrates: I saw that water bag even after a year."
"1281","I do not find in what has been revealed to me anything forbidden..."" until the end of the verse. (Then the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said:) There is no harm in it; tan its skin and benefit from it. The narrator says: Then we sent it to that woman, so she tanned its skin and made a water bag from it until it wore out."
"1282","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) passed by a dead goat and said: Why do you not benefit from its skin? The people said: O Messenger of Allah! It is dead. The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Its consumption has been declared unlawful."
"1283","The noble wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him), Sayyidah Maymunah (may Allah be pleased with her), informed me of this: One of her goats died, so the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Why do you not tan its skin and benefit from it?"
"1284","The Prophet ﷺ saw a dead sheep which had been given in charity to a freed slave-girl of Maimuna, the wife of the Prophet ﷺ . The Prophet ﷺ said, ""Why don't you get the benefit of its hide?"" They said, ""It is dead."" He replied, ""Only to eat (its meat) is illegal."" (Using translation from Bukhārī 1492)"
"1285","“Why don’t they take its skin and ten it, and make us of it?” They said: “O Messenger of Allah, it is dead meat.”* He said: “It is only unlawful to eat it.” (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 3610)"
"1286","the Messenger of Allah ordered that the hides of dead animals be made use of if they had been tanned. (Daif) (Using translation from Nasāʾī 4252)"
"1287","“I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: ‘Any skin that has been tanned has been purified.’” (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 3609)"
"1288","“I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: ‘Any skin that has been tanned has been purified.’” (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 3609)"
"1289","The people said: It is dead. The Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) said: Its consumption has been declared unlawful."
"1290","Sayyidah Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: The Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) said: ""The tanning of the hide of a dead animal makes it pure."
"1291","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said to them: Why do you not take its skin? The people said: It is dead. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Water and the leaves of qaradh will purify it."""
"1292","I remember this about the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took water from the well present in their house with a bucket and rinsed his mouth with it."
"1293","I was in the state of menstruation, I would place a vessel to my mouth, then I would pass it to the Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him), and he would place his blessed mouth at the same spot where I had placed my mouth. While I was in the state of menstruation, I would take a bone (with meat on it), eat from it, then pass it to the Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him), and he would place his mouth at the same spot where I had placed my mouth."
"1294","The Messenger of Allah said: ""If a dog licks the vessel of anyome of you, let him wash it seven times."" (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 364)"
"1295","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The way to purify the vessel of any person when a dog has licked it is to wash it seven times."
"1296","""The Messenger of Allah said: 'If a dog licks the vessel of anyone of you, let him wash it seven times.'"" (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 366)"
"1297","The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: The purification of the utensil belonging to any one of you, after it is licked by a dog, lies in washing it seven times, using sand for the first time. (Using translation from Muslim 279d)"
"1298","The Messenger of Allah said: 'If a dog licks a vessel, wash it seven times and rub it with dust the eight times."" (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 365)"
"1299","Kabshah, daughter of Ka'b ibn Malik and wife of Ibn AbuQatadah, reported: AbuQatadah visited (me) and I poured out water for him for ablution. A cat came and drank some of it and he tilted the vessel for it until it drank some of it. Kabshah said: He saw me looking at him; he asked me: Are you surprised, my niece? I said: Yes. He then reported the Messenger of Allah ﷺ as saying: It is not unclean; it is one of those (males or females) who go round among you. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 75)"
"1300","""We went out with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on one of his journeys, and when we were in Al-Baida' or Dhat Al-Jaish, a necklace of mine broke and fell. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ stayed there looking for it and the people stayed with him. There was no water near them, and they did not have water with them. The people came to Abu Bakr, may Allah be pleased with him, and said: 'Do you see what 'Aishah has done? She has made the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and the people stop and they are not near any water and they do not have water with them.' Abu Bakr, may Allah be pleased with him, came while the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was resting his head on my thigh and had gone to sleep. He said: 'You have detained the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and the people, and they are not near any water and they do not have any water with them.'"" 'Aishah said: ""Abu Bakr rebuked me and said whatever Allah willed he would say. He started poking me on my hip, and the only thing that prevented me from moving was the fact that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was resting on my thigh. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ slept until morning when he woke up without any water. Then Allah, the Mighty and Sublime revealed the verse of Tayammum. Usaid bin Hudair said: 'This is not the first time we have been blessed because of you, O family of Abu Bakr!'"" She said: ""Then we made the camel that I had been riding stand up, and we found the necklace beneath it."" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 310)"
"1301","Sayyiduna Imran bin Husain (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: We were traveling with the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him). We traveled throughout the night, and when the last part of the night came, sleep overcame us, and for a traveler, nothing is dearer than sleep. The heat of the sun woke us up. Sayyiduna Imran (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The first among those who woke up was such-and-such person, then such-and-such person, and then such-and-such person. The narr"
"1302","Sayyiduna Imran bin Husain (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: We were traveling with the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him). When the last part of the night came, we fell asleep, and for a traveler, nothing is dearer than sleep. The heat of the sun woke us up. So-and-so, so-and-so, and so-and-so woke up—Abu Raja, the narrator, mentioned their names, but ‘Awf, another narrator, forgot them. The fourth person to wake up was Sayyiduna Umar bin Khattab (may Allah be pleased with him)."
"1303","I asked the Prophet ﷺ about tayammum. He commanded me to strike only one stroke (i.e. the strike the ground) for (wiping) the face and the hands. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 327)"
"1304","The narrator named Ya'la has narrated this, A'mash has narrated this, I said to Shaqiq: This ruling is only for him."",""I have not seen Umar compromising on this. He said"",""'What will you do with this verse: """"So if you do not find water"","" then purify yourselves with clean earth""""?' He said"","" 'If we granted permission to them in this matter"","" then whenever one of them found cold water"","" he would perform tayammum with the earth.' Ya'la narrated this from Al-A'mash who said"","" 'I said to my brother (Ammar)"","" """"This was only because of this.""""'"""
"1305","Sayyiduna Abu Musa Ash'ari (may Allah be pleased with him) said to Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Mas'ud (may Allah be pleased with him): If a person"
"1306","Sayyiduna Umar bin Khattab (may Allah be pleased with him) and said: I have become junub (in a state of major ritual impurity),"
"1307","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) sent me and you on an expedition. I became junub. I rolled in the earth and then I came to the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) and informed him about this, so he said: It would have been sufficient for you to do like this. Then he (the Prophet) wiped his face and both arms once. Upon this, Sayyiduna Abdullah said: I did not see that Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) was satisfied with this. So Sayyiduna Abu Musa Ash'ari (may Allah be pleased with him) said: Then what do you say about this verse: ""And if you do not find water, then perform tayammum with clean earth."" So Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Mas'ud (may Allah be pleased with him) said: If we start giving people concession in this matter, then if any one of them finds the water cold, he will perform wiping with earth. The narrator named A'mash says: I said to Shaqiq: Did he (Sayyiduna Ibn Mas'ud) dislike it for this reason?"
"1308","I asked the Prophet ﷺ about tayammum. He commanded me to strike only one stroke (i.e. the strike the ground) for (wiping) the face and the hands. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 327)"
"1309","A man came to 'Umar bin khattab and said: ""I became impure following sexual emission and cannot find any water."" 'Umar said to him: ""Do not pray."" But 'Ammar bin Yasir said: ""Do you not remember, O Commander of the Believers, when you and I were on a military expedition and we became sexually impure and could not find water? As for you, you did not pray, but I rolled in the dust and then prayed. When I came to the Prophet and told him what had happened, he said: 'It would have been enough for you (to do this).' (Then demonstrating) the Prophet struck the ground with his hands, then blew on hem, and wiped his face and palms with them."" (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 569)"
"1310","narrates: We performed tayammum up to the shoulders along with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). (Imam Ibn Hibban, may Allah have mercy on him, says:) This was at the time when the verse regarding the command of tayammum had been revealed, but the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had not yet taught Sayyiduna Ammar (may Allah be pleased with him) the method of tayammum. Then afterwards, while teaching him, he explained that for the face and both hands, only one strike will be made. This was when Sayyiduna Ammar (may Allah be pleased with him) had asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about tayammum."
"1311","A few goats got collected with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He said: Abu Dharr, drive them to the wood. I drove them to Rabadhah (a place near Medina). I would have sexual defilement (during my stay there) and I would remain (in this condition) for five or six days. Then I came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He said: O Abu Dharr. I kept silence. He then said: May your mother bereave you, Abu Dharr: woe be to your mother. He then called a black slave-girl for me. She brought a vessel which contained water. She then concealed me by drawing a curtain and I concealed myself behind a she-camel, and took a bath. I felt as if I had thrown away a mountain from me. He said: Clean earth is a means for ablution for a Muslim, even for ten years (he does not find water); but when you find water, you should make it touch your skin, for that is better. The version of Musaddad has: ""the goats (were collected) from the alms,"" and the tradition reported by 'Amr is complete. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 332)"
"1312","I took them and came to the place of Rabadhah. The narrator states: I remained in a state of major ritual impurity (janabah) for five or six days. I felt very uneasy. I presented myself before the Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him). At that time, he was sitting leaning against the chamber. When he saw me, he asked: O Abu Dharr, what has happened to you? The narrator says: I sat down. The Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) asked: O Abu Dharr, what has happened to you? May your mother weep for you! I said: O Messenger of Allah! I have become junub (in a state of major ritual impurity). The narrator says: Then the Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) ordered a black slave girl, and she brought a vessel of water. I made a curtain of cloth behind a camel and performed ghusl (ritual bath), and I felt as if a mountain had been lifted from me. The Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) said: Come forward. Pure earth is a means of purification for a Muslim, even if ten years pass. Then when he finds water, he should let it touch his skin (i.e., he should perform ghusl)."
"1313","""The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Clean earth is the Wudu' of the Muslim, even if he does not find water for ten years.'"" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 322)"
"1314","narrates: A man became junub (in a state of major ritual impurity) during the winter season. He inquired about the ruling, and he was instructed to perform ghusl (ritual bath). (Due to performing ghusl, he passed away.) This matter was mentioned before the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him), so he said: ""Why did the people cause his death? May Allah destroy those people."" He said this three times. (Then he said:) ""Allah the Exalted has made earth (the narrator is in doubt, perhaps these are the words) tayammum a means of attaining purity."" This doubt in the wording of the narration is from Abdullah bin Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both). After that, he mentioned it without any doubt."
"1315","I had a wet dream,"" so he washed his private parts and performed ablution as for prayer, and led the people in prayer. When he presented himself before the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him), the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) asked his companions, ""How did you find Amr and his companions?"" The people praised him and mentioned this matter. ""O Messenger of Allah, he led us in prayer while in a state of major ritual impurity."" So the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) called Sayyiduna Amr and asked him, and Sayyiduna Amr informed him and told him about the cold he had faced. He said, ""O Messenger of Allah! Allah Almighty has said: 'Do not kill yourselves.' If I had performed ghusl, I would have died."" The Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) laughed at the statement of Sayyiduna Amr."
"1316","The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came from the privy. A man met him near Bir Jamal and saluted him. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ did not return the salutation until he came to a wall and placed his hands on the wall and wiped his face and hands; he then returned the man's salutation. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 331)"
"1317","I did not move because the Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) was sleeping with his head in my lap. Then, when the Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) woke up, it was morning and there was no water. So Allah Almighty revealed the verse regarding the command of tayammum (dry ablution), and the people performed tayammum. Upon this, Usaid bin Hudair, who was one of the leaders, said: O family of Abu Bakr, this is not your first blessing. Lady Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: The camel I was riding, when we made it stand up, we found the necklace underneath it."
"1318","Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) about wiping over leather socks (khuffs), so he informed that the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) used to wipe over the leather socks."
"1319","The angels, being pleased with the action of the seeker of knowledge, spread their wings for him."" I asked him about wiping over the socks, so he informed me that the Messenger of Allah had commanded that when we are traveling, we may wipe for three days, and when we are residing, for one day and night. We would remove them when performing ablution due to defecation, urination, or sleep (but in the case of major impurity, they should be removed and the feet washed)."
"1320","Sayyiduna Safwan bin Assal Muradi. I said: I have some confusion in my mind regarding wiping over the leather socks"
"1321","Sayyiduna Safwan bin Assal Muradi. He inquired: Why have you come? I replied: For the acquisition of knowledge. He s"
"1322","The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) granted us the concession that a traveler may wipe over the leather socks for three days, and a resident for one day and one night."
"1323","""The Messenger of Allah ﷺ and Bilal entered Al-Aswaf [1] and he went to relieve himself and then came out."" Usamah said: ""I asked Bilal: 'What did he do?' Bilal said: 'The Prophet ﷺ went to relieve himself, then he performed Wudu', so he washed his hands and face, and wiped his head and he wiped over his Khuffs, then prayed.'"" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 120)"
"1324","The Prophet granted a concession to travelers: ""If a traveler performed ablution and put on leather socks, then he performed a fresh ablution, he could wipe over the leather socks for three days and nights; the resident could do so for one day and one night."" (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 556)"
"1325","I presented myself before Safwan bin Assal Muradi. He inquired: Why have you come? I replied: To seek knowledge. He said: I heard the Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) say: ""Whoever sets out from his house to seek knowledge, the angels, being pleased with his action, spread their wings for him."" Zirr said: I have come to ask about wiping over leather socks (khuffs). He replied: Yes, we were in an army which the Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) had dispatched, and he instructed us that when we put on the leather socks in a state of purity (i.e., after performing ablution), we may wipe over them for three days during travel. After relieving ourselves (urinating or defecating), we would not remove them while performing ablution."
"1326","I saw the Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) perform ablution. He washed his face and both arms, then wiped over his socks. I said: O Messenger of Allah, are you wiping over your socks? He replied: I put my feet into them while I was in a state of ablution."
"1327","Sayyiduna Ali bin Abi Talib (may Allah be pleased with him) about wiping over the leather socks (khuffs). He replied: Allah's Messenger granted us permission to wipe over the leather socks for one day and one night in the state of residence, and for three days and three nights for the traveler."
"1328","The Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) prescribed the duration for wiping over the leather socks as three days and three nights for a traveler, and one day and one night for a resident."
"1329","""The Messenger of Allah set a time limit for the traveler of three days, and if the questioner had persisted in asking, he would have made it five (days)."" (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 553)"
"1330","The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) was asked about wiping over the leather socks (khuffs), so he (peace and blessings be upon him) said: For the traveler, three days and three nights, and for the resident, one day is permitted for wiping."
"1331","The Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""For the traveler, three days and three nights, and for the resident, one day and one night."" (Imam Ibn Hibban, may Allah have mercy on him, says:) This narration has been transmitted as a marfu' hadith from Shu'bah only by Yahya al-Qattan and Abu Walid Tayalisi."
"1332","The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) granted permission. (While traveling) we could wipe (over the socks) for three days. If we had requested more (concession), he would have granted us more."
"1333","narrates: A Bedouin asked the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) about wiping (over socks), so he said: For a traveler, three days and three nights, and for a resident, one day and one night."
"1334","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) was asked: O Messenger of Allah! What is your opinion about a person who loses his ablution and then performs ablution, wipes over his leather socks, and offers prayer? The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: There is no harm in it."
"1335","""We prayed with Abdullah bin Mas'ud in his house. He stood between us and we placed our hands on our knees, but he took them off and made us interlace our fingers, and said: ""I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ do that.'"" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 1030)"
"1336","Sayyiduna Jarir bin Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him) that after urinating, he performed ablution and wiped over his socks, then stood up and offered prayer. He was asked about this, so he said: I saw the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) doing this. Ibrahim Nakha'i says: This narration was very much liked by those people because Sayyiduna Jarir (may Allah be pleased with him) had accepted Islam during the lifetime of the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him)."
"1337","""Jarir bin 'Abdullah urinated, then he performed ablution and wiped over his leather socks. Someone asked him: 'Do you do this?' He said: 'Why shouldn't I? I saw the Messenger of Allah doing this.'"" Ibrahim (who narrated it from Hammam) said: ""They were pleased by the Hadith of Jarir because he accepted Islam after the revelation of Ma'idah."" (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 543)"
"1338","The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wiped over his socks and shoes while performing ablution. The narrator Abu Qais Awdi’s"
"1339","Sayyiduna Aws bin Abu Aws (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: I saw my father wiping over his shoes while performing ablution. I objected to his action and said: Are you wiping over your shoes? He replied: I saw the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) wiping over them."""
"1340","We prayed Zuhr with ‘Ali ؓ , then he went to a gathering that he used to hold in ar-Rahbah. He sat and we sat around him, then the time for ‘Asr came. A vessel (of water) was brought to him. He took a handful from it and rinsed his mouth and nose, and he wiped his face and forearms, and he wiped his head, and he wiped his feet. Then he stood up and drank what was left over in the vessel. Then he said: I have been told that some men dislike anyone to drink whilst standing, but I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ do what I have done. (Using translation from Aḥmad 1366)"
"1341","I have done, and this is the ablution of a person who has not lost his previous ablution."
"1342","The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wiped over his forehead and his turban, and he wiped over his leather socks."
"1343","narrates from his father that he saw the Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) performing ablution and wiping over his turban and leather socks."
"1344","Sayyiduna Salman al-Farsi (may Allah be pleased with him). He saw a man who had become without wudu, and as he was about to remove his socks to perform wudu, Sayyiduna Salman said to him: Wipe over them (the socks) and over your turban, for I have seen the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) wiping over his cloak and his socks."
"1345","""I saw the Messenger of Allah wiping over his leather socks and turban."" (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 562)"
"1346","I have also heard this narration from the son of Sayyiduna Mughira bin Shu’bah (may Allah be pleased with him). (Imam Ibn Hibban, may Allah have mercy on him, says:) These words, “He wiped over his forehead and his turban,” have caused confusion for the one who does not have expertise in the science of hadith, and he believes that it is not permissible to wipe over the turban without wiping the forehead. This person has considered the narration transmitted from Amr bin Umayyah as an explanatory narration for this hadith. That is, the narration in which the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wiped over his turban along with his forehead takes precedence over the narration in which only the forehead is mentioned apart from the turban, because the forehead is part of the head. However, by the grace and mercy of Allah, this is not the case; rather, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wiped over his head during ablution, and he also wiped over his turban without wiping the forehead, and he wiped over both the forehead and the turban. So these are three separate incidents on three different occasions. One may act upon any one of these Sunnahs, and it is not necessary to make one Sunnah obligatory and consider acting upon the other as disliked."
"1347","I replied: ""Yes, I do."" I brought a water container to your service. The Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) washed both his hands and face. When he began to wash his arms, the sleeve of his cloak was tight, so he took his arm out from underneath and placed the cloak on his shoulder. Then he washed both his arms, then wiped over his socks and turban. Then he mounted (his ride), and I also mounted with him. We reached the people, and Sayyiduna Abdur Rahman bin Awf had already led them in one rak'ah (unit of prayer). When he sensed the arrival of the Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him), he began to move back. But the Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) said: ""Continue leading the prayer."" When Sayyiduna Abdur Rahman bin Awf (may Allah be pleased with him) completed the prayer, the Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) and Sayyiduna Mughirah stood up and performed the rak'ah that they had missed earlier."
"1348","The Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) said: The blood of menstruation is black and recognizable. When it is that, then refrain from prayer, and when it is of another color, then perform ablution and start offering prayer."
"1349","""A woman asked 'Aishah: 'Should a menstruating woman make up the Salah she misses? She said: 'Are you a Haruri? [1] We used to menstruate during the time of Messenger of Allah ﷺ but we did not make up the missed Salah nor were we commanded to do so.'"" [1] Meaning are you one of the Khawarij. Harura is a place associated with a group of the Khawarij. (Using translation from Nasāʾī 382)"
"1350","""Fatimah bint Abi Hubaish said to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ: 'O Messenger of Allah ﷺ, I do not become pure. Should I stop praying? The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'That is a vein and is not menstruation. When your period comes, stop praying, and when the same amount of time as your regular period has passed, then wash the blood from yourself and pray.'"" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 218)"
"1351","The Prophet (peace be upon him) said to her: This is not menstruation, rather it is blood from another vein. Perform ghusl and offer prayer. Lady Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates, so Umm Habibah bint Jahsh used to perform ghusl for every prayer. She would sit in a tub, and the redness of the blood would dominate the water, then she would offer prayer."
